        "problem": "$\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-{180}^{\u2218})=$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v={180}^{\u2218},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-{180}^{\u2218}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{180}^{\u2218}+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{180}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot (-1)+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
